Stops evaluating visitor-submitted form values as email template source.

Problem: every form submission builds the admin and customer notification
bodies (also when notifications and saving entries are disabled, because the
success message path initialises the entry). The submission overview table in
those bodies passed each submitted value through Entry::filterVar(), which runs
Magento\Email\Model\Template\Filter::filter() with the value as the template
text. Template directives typed into any form field by an anonymous visitor
were therefore processed server-side (template injection). The values are only
escaped with htmlspecialchars() in Submit::cleanParam(), which leaves {{ }}
intact.

Root cause: Entry::getFilteredSubmissionParamsForTable() used
$this->filterVar($param) for the submitted value.
Fix: use the submitted value as data. It is already HTML-escaped by
Submit::cleanParam(), so the overview table template keeps receiving escaped
output. Pre-filled customer values do not rely on this call, they are resolved
when the form is rendered (Block\Form\Widget\View::getFormHtml() and
PrivateContentFilter). filterVar() is still used for admin-configured values
(recipient name/e-mail, notification fields).

diff --git a/Model/Entry.php b/Model/Entry.php
index 1cd30ae..2faeb67 100644
--- a/Model/Entry.php
+++ b/Model/Entry.php
@@ -356,7 +356,10 @@ class Entry extends \Magento\Framework\Model\AbstractModel implements EntryInter
             }
             $params[$key] = [
                 'label' => $this->getFieldLabel($key),
-                'value' => $this->filterVar($param)
+                // BEGIN PATCH
+                // 'value' => $this->filterVar($param)
+                'value' => $param
+                // END PATCH
             ];
         }
         return $params;
